                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fa0e32eb-48ec-38e7-9e72-dfcae42c0333",
                        "entry_id": "270bc30a-1153-3ead-acd9-ef8b3f1329d0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One side's (from when the first player begins to bat, until the last player is out) or individual player's turn to bat or the runs scored during those durations."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3e42d936-7121-3002-958d-b0caeab16ff1",
                        "entry_id": "270bc30a-1153-3ead-acd9-ef8b3f1329d0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A comparable period of play in croquet or roque."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d8959116-9e01-34d6-9f39-a067eb9f35be",
                        "entry_id": "270bc30a-1153-3ead-acd9-ef8b3f1329d0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The time during which any party is in possession of power, or enjoying good luck, etc.; a turn of any kind."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "British"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cd3fe829-2a18-33fb-93f2-5914f15fb239",
                        "entry_id": "270bc30a-1153-3ead-acd9-ef8b3f1329d0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person's lifespan."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "British",
                            "euphemistic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0fe6f536-2955-4a94-bc5b-4d45e3e12101",
                                "sense_id": "cd3fe829-2a18-33fb-93f2-5914f15fb239",
                                "text": "Forty-odd. That's a better innings than Mozart's thirty-five. Only a moderate knock perhaps in an era brimming with space age technology, and transplants, and artificial hips etcet, but still higher than Mozart's."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "20282e3e-3c62-4ed9-90e4-39add92a9878",
                                "sense_id": "cd3fe829-2a18-33fb-93f2-5914f15fb239",
                                "text": "My mother-in-law died at 89 years of age, while sad and as you might expect, we used the phrase “she had a good innings”."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "158c9b01-8f0b-4afc-a300-67c46178ffac",
                                "sense_id": "cd3fe829-2a18-33fb-93f2-5914f15fb239",
                                "text": "He was the first of my grandparents to die but none of them made it much past seventy, although that was very much looked on as 'a decent innings' in early-seventies England."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6ca1bf8-5109-479d-b44f-20b116d667f8",
                                "sense_id": "cd3fe829-2a18-33fb-93f2-5914f15fb239",
                                "text": "You can only say, she had a good innings, so many times. I suppose seventy nine isn't so bad. It's a damn sight more than I can expect."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "87428515-0be8-4aae-b40f-7a441921a7ff",
                                "sense_id": "cd3fe829-2a18-33fb-93f2-5914f15fb239",
                                "text": "Like father, like son. Sixty-eight. Not such a bad innings, really, when the old man was gone at fifty-three."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
